\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Notation}
\title{Notation for structure}
\date{2026-11-13}

\p{The Kähler–Dirac operator is #{\extD=\extd+\extdag}.
On cochains the same operator is #{\extD=\covwedge+\extdag}
(\ref{fdip-00OL}).}

\p{A Pauli product carries the complex unit #{\ui}
(\ref{fdip-009E}, \ref{fdip-00RS}).}

\p{The Kähler–Dirac operator #{\extD} is kept distinct from
#{D} and #{\extd}. It is used where a statement needs a
self-adjoint first-order operator; a statement that does not
is written with #{\cov}.}
